ient-all` is the shaded/uber jar combining `pulsar-client` + `pulsar-client-admin` — it's the actual connecting implementation (binary protocol, producer/consumer, connection pooling), unlike the sibling Pulsar artifacts already in this repo (`pulsar-client-api`, `pulsar-client-admin-api`, `pulsar-common`, `pulsar-package-core`), which are interface/utility layers whose existing tests never touch the network.\n- Unlike Kafka (which ships an embedded-broker test-jar used by the existing `kafka-clients` tests), Pulsar has no lightweight in-process broker artifact — the ecosystem-standard way to test against it, per Apache's own docs and the dedicated Testcontainers Pulsar module, is a standalone broker in Docker (ports 6650 binary, 8080 HTTP admin).\n- No Pulsar image is currently pinned under `tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/allowed-docker-images/`, and this repo's `checkAllowedDockerImages` gate means the generation agent can't just invent one — it has to be allow-listed in advance, which is exactly what this decision step is for.\n- I found a concrete precedent of extra JVM module-access flags needed for this exact library family: `pulsar-common`'s `build.gradle` already needs `--add-exports=java.management/sun.management=ALL-UNNAMED`, `--add-opens=java.management/sun.management=ALL-UNNAMED`, and `--add-exports=java.security.jgss/sun.security.krb5=ALL-UNNAMED` on both the JVM test run and the native-image test binary. Since `pulsar-client-all` shades that same code in, this is worth flagging as something to try if tests fail on module access.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"pulsar-client-all is the real network-connecting Pulsar client (shaded pulsar-client+pulsar-client-admin); unlike its already-supported sibling Pulsar API/utility artifacts, meaningful coverage of its binary-protocol, producer/consumer and connection code requires a live broker, and Pulsar has no embedded-broker test artifact (unlike Kafka) — the ecosystem-standard route is a Docker broker.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n      \"image\": \"apachepulsar/pulsar:4.2.5\",\n      \"slug\": \"apachepulsar_pulsar\",\n      \"reason\": \"No Pulsar broker image is currently allow-listed. A live standalone broker is needed to exercise pulsar-client-all's producer/consumer/admin round trip; without it, generated tests can only reach builder/config construction, as the existing pulsar-client-api and pulsar-client-admin-api tests already show is possible without a broker.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Follow the same pattern already used for postgresql/mariadb/mysql tests: `docker run --rm -d -p 127.0.0.1::6650 -p 127.0.0.1::8080 apachepulsar/pulsar:4.2.5 bin/pulsar standalone --advertised-address localhost`, resolve the two mapped host ports via `docker inspect`, and poll for readiness (retry building a PulsarClient/producer, or GET the admin port's /admin/v2/clusters) with Awaitility before running tests; tear the container down in @AfterAll. Make sure at least one test does a real producer-send/consumer-receive (and ideally a PulsarAdmin call) against the container so the shaded netty/protobuf and connection-pool code paths are actually reached, not just builder construction. If the JVM test run or native-image test binary fails on a module-access error, try the same flags already needed by the sibling pulsar-common artifact: --add-exports=java.management/sun.management=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.management/sun.management=ALL-UNNAMED, and --add-exports=java.security.jgss/sun.security.krb5=ALL-UNNAMED, on both tasks.withType(Test) and graalvmNative.binaries.test.buildArgs.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Pulsar standalone bundles ZooKeeper/BookKeeper/broker in one JVM and can take 30-60s+ to report ready; a short readiness timeout will flake.\",\n    \"If generated tests end up only calling builder/config APIs without a real send/receive, the Docker setup is wasted and coverage will look like the existing API-only pulsar-client-api/pulsar-client-admin-api tests — review should confirm an actual round trip is exercised.\",\n    \"apachepulsar/pulsar:4.2.5 matches the tested client version; if that exact tag is ever removed from Docker Hub, the nearest 4.2.x maintenance tag is an acceptable substitute.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":9091,"type":"result","duration_ms":264278,"uuid":"7680737a-00b8-4062-94b1-160290929960","ttft_stream_ms":2258,"time_to_request_ms":140,"first_content_frame_ms":2259,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

